-###  Generated by the OWL API (version 4.5.29.2024-05-13T12:11:03Z) https://github.com/owlcs/owlapi
+#################################################################
+#    Alignments to the Data Privacy Vocabulary (DPV 2.x)
+#
+#    AIDOC-AP grounds its Annex IV terms in DPV (core, AI, AI Act, TECH).
+#    AIDOC-AP terms are Annex IV-scoped SPECIALISATIONS of the broader DPV
+#    concepts, so we assert rdfs:subClassOf (AIDOC subClassOf DPV) rather
+#    than owl:equivalentClass: adding Annex IV documentation constraints
+#    narrows the extension, which co-extensional equivalence would
+#    misrepresent. Where there is no clean subsumption (same concept, or DPV
+#    is the narrower term) we use SKOS mapping relations. Curated starting
+#    set; extended as further correspondences pass the alignment curation.
+#################################################################
+
+# AIDOC-AP is the narrower, Annex IV-scoped specialisation of the DPV class:
+:AISystem rdfs:subClassOf dpv-ai:AISystem .
+:AIModel rdfs:subClassOf dpv-ai:Model .
+:Standard rdfs:subClassOf dpv:Standard .
+:AIProvider rdfs:subClassOf dpv-aiact:AIProvider .
+:AIDeployer rdfs:subClassOf dpv-aiact:AIDeployer .
+:TechnicalDocumentation rdfs:subClassOf dpv-aiact:TechnicalDocumentation .
+
+# Concept-level correspondences without a clean subsumption:
+:Auditor skos:closeMatch dpv-tech:Auditor .
+:HumanOversightMechanism skos:closeMatch dpv:HumanOversight .
+# DPV's EU declaration of conformity is the narrower (EU-specific) term:
+:DeclarationOfConformity skos:narrowMatch dpv-aiact:EUDeclarationOfConformity .
